      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T11:08:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think output index has anything to do with uniform index.\nNote that there are two kinds of indices:\n- the texture indices which are used to bind the source textures.\n- the output indices are the indices of the dest textures.\nThe current code use the same index numbers for both but we don\u0027t have to do that.\nMy suggestion is that we bind the source textures starting from index 1.\nNot that we should bind the output location starting from 1.\n\nWe should do something like this:\n```\n    finalStream \u003c\u003c absl::StrFormat(\n        \"struct Params {\\n\"\n        \"offset: vec2i,\\n\"\n        \"};\\n\"\n        \"@group(0) @binding(0) var\u003cuniform\u003e params : Params;\\n\";\n        \n    for (auto i : pipelineKey.attachmentsToExpandResolve) {\n        // Bind the src texture starting from index 1\n        auto inputIdx \u003d i + 1;\n        // Retain the output indices.\n        auto outputIdx \u003d i;\n        finalStream \u003c\u003c absl::StrFormat(\"@group(0) @binding(%u) var srcTex%u : texture_2d\u003cf32\u003e;\\n\",\n                                       inputIdx, inputIdx);\n\n        outputStructStream \u003c\u003c absl::StrFormat(\"@location(%u) output%u : vec4f,\\n\", outputIdx, outputIdx);\n        assignOutputsStream \u003c\u003c absl::StrFormat(\n            \"\\toutputColor.output%u \u003d textureLoad(srcTex%u, vec2i(position.xy) + \"\n            \"params.offset, 0);\\n\",\n            outputIdx, inputIdx);\n    }\n```\n\nThis will require changing the binding logic in `GetOrCreateExpandMultisamplePipeline` and BindGroup creation also. You can move some duplicated code to a common function for both expand \u0026 resolve.",
      "parentUuid": "a8dde9d9_2a1e0fad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 86,
        "endChar": 22
      },
