      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T11:08:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by \"the scissor are the same\".\n\n`{0, 0, colorAttachmentWidth, colorAttachmentHeight}` is not the same as `{rect-\u003ecolorOffsetX, rect-\u003ecolorOffsetY, rect-\u003ewidth, rect-\u003eheight}`. is it?\n\nWe have to do that because the current spec of `dawn-partial-load-resolve-texture` doesn\u0027t say that all the draws have to be within the `expandResolveRect`. It only says that the expanding and the resolve have to be done in that region. If we don\u0027t restore the scissor rect, every subsequent user draw will be constrained inside the `expandResolveRect` only. See our discussion here https://chromium.slack.com/archives/C087HTPGJG2/p1742900620106219?thread_ts\u003d1742887711.096209\u0026cid\u003dC087HTPGJG2",
      "parentUuid": "d05dc20f_9a26c452",
